socrates: fDeviceInit for the ABL handoff - TUR CHECK-CONDITIONs until the
device's bring-up flag is set (flash #7's Plan B verdict, 2026-11-07).

With the shim's pre-XNU wake compiled out (Plan B), the ABL's handoff
arrives at bsd_init with the link UP - the kernel's ready gate passes and
no wake runs - but the device still sits in needs-init state: TUR
CHECK-CONDITIONs on all three unit-attention retries (response 0x1,
status 0x2), the exact behavior of the shim's M2 first flash. The v19
cure applies here too: SET fDeviceInit, poll until the device clears it,
then give the TUR another chance.

The retry lives in its own block between the first TUR loop and the
partition lookup; the 00xx patches own that function's interior, so this
rides after the series instead of editing 0028 (whose context 0030/0034
patch byte-for-byte).
---
bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c | 12 ++++++++++++
1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -852,6 +852,19 @@
 		for (int i = 0; i < 3 && (error = ufs_scsi(tur, sizeof(tur), 0, false)); i++) {
 		}
 	}
+	if (error) {
+		/* socrates flash #7 (Plan B, 2026-11-07): the ABL's handoff leaves the
+		 * link UP (the ready gate passes, no wake needed) but the device still
+		 * in needs-init state - TUR CHECK-CONDITIONs (response 0x1, status 0x2)
+		 * on every retry, exactly the M2 first-flash behavior. The shim's v19
+		 * cure: SET fDeviceInit, poll until the device clears it, retry TUR. */
+		error = ufs_dev_init();
+		if (!error) {
+			static const uint8_t tur2[6] = { 0x00 };
+			for (int i = 0; i < 3 && (error = ufs_scsi(tur2, sizeof(tur2), 0, false)); i++) {
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	if (!error) {
 		error = ufs_find_partition(want);
 	}
